B.c0b=s(["Vienna Convention Art. 36","StPO \xa7114b(2)","EU Directive 2013/48/EU Art. 6"],t.s)
B.b2O=new A.C("Consular Access","Consular notification required upon arrest. Germany has established procedures given high foreign prisoner numbers. All 16 federal states implement Vienna Convention consistently.",null)
B.bTt=s(["GG Art. 103","StPO \xa7187","EU Directive 2010/64/EU"],t.s)
B.b2k=new A.C("Right to Interpreter","Free interpreter from police questioning through trial. Germany has extensive interpreter infrastructure. Translation of essential documents including indictment and judgment.",null)
B.bNp=s(["IRG (Gesetz \xfcber internationale Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen)","EU Framework Decision 2008/909/JHA","CoE Convention ETS 112"],t.s)
B.b5B=new A.C("Transfer to Home Country","FD 2008/909/JHA implemented via IRG (International Legal Assistance in Criminal Matters Act). Germany is one of the most active states for prisoner transfers. Bilateral agreements with many non-EU countries.",null)
B.c2t=s(["StPO \xa7\xa7140-142","EU Directive 2016/1919/EU"],t.s)
B.b3g=new A.C("Legal Aid","Pflichtverteidiger (mandatory defence counsel) appointed when: offence carries 1+ year minimum, pre-trial detention, complex case, or if accused cannot defend themselves. Prozesskostenhilfe for other cases. Free for detained persons.",null)
B.c2n=s(["16 State Prison Acts (Landesstrafvollzugsgesetze)","European Prison Rules"],t.s)
B.b1D=new A.C("Prison Conditions","Standards vary by federal state but generally good. Single cells the norm. Comprehensive activities, education, and work programmes. Each state has its own prison act (Strafvollzugsgesetz). CPT generally positive.",null)
B.bPV=s(["State Prison Acts","StPO \xa7148 (lawyer access)"],t.s)
B.b3a=new A.C("Communication Rights","At least one visit per month (1 hour). Phone calls available. Letters unrestricted for sentenced prisoners. Long-term visits in some states. Lawyer visits unrestricted and confidential.",null)
B.bTs=s(["State Prison Acts (healthcare chapters)"],t.s)
B.b2H=new A.C("Healthcare","Healthcare provided by prison medical service. Equivalent to community standard required. Justizvollzugskrankenhaus (prison hospitals) in larger states. Drug substitution therapy available. Mental health care provided.",null)
B.bNT=s(["GG Art. 4","State Prison Acts"],t.s)
B.b2z=new A.C("Religious Rights","Catholic, Protestant, and Muslim chaplains in most prisons. Other faiths accommodated. Religious diet available (halal, kosher). Prayer rooms provided.",null)
B.bJU=s(["AufenthG \xa7\xa753-56 (Aufenthaltsgesetz)","Freiz\xfcgG/EU \xa76 (EU citizens)"],t.s)
B.b2o=new A.C("Immigration Consequences","Criminal conviction triggers mandatory review by Ausl\xe4nderbeh\xf6rde (foreigners authority). Sentence of 1+ year typically leads to loss of residence permit. Entry ban (Einreiseverbot) up to 10 years. EU citizens: only for serious public policy/security threats.","Challenge Ausweisung (expulsion) at Verwaltungsgericht (Administrative Court). Art. 8 ECHR and family ties are key defences. Long-term residents have stronger protection.")
B.bYl=s(["StGB \xa7\xa757-57a","StPO \xa7456a"],t.s)
B.b3C=new A.C("Early Release / Parole","Conditional release (Aussetzung der Reststrafe) after two-thirds (standard) or half (exceptional, for first sentences under 2 years). Foreign prisoners eligible. \xa7456a StPO allows early release of foreigners for deportation (Absehen von Vollstreckung).","\xa7456a StPO is frequently used: prosecution can suspend remaining sentence to enable deportation, typically after half the sentence. This can be advantageous (earlier release) or disadvantageous (no parole supervision, immediate deportation).")
B.bKv=s(["AufenthG \xa7\xa758-62","StPO \xa7456a","EU Return Directive 2008/115/EC"],t.s)
B.b6d=new A.C("Deportation After Sentence","Ausl\xe4nderbeh\xf6rde issues Abschiebungsanordnung. \xa7456a StPO allows suspension of sentence for deportation. Detention pending removal (Abschiebungshaft) if needed. Non-refoulement via \xa760 AufenthG. Duldung (toleration) if deportation not possible.",null)
B.bTL=s(["IRG \xa7\xa778-83","GG Art. 16(2)","EU Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA"],t.s)
B.b3f=new A.C("European Arrest Warrant","Oberlandesgericht (Higher Regional Court) handles EAW. German nationals can be surrendered (GG Art. 16(2) amended 2000). Germany is a major user of the EAW system.",null)
