B.b4P=new A.C("Consular Access","Right to consular contact upon arrest. Greece has one of the highest foreign prisoner percentages in the EU. Large numbers of Albanian, Pakistani, and Nigerian nationals.",null)
B.bRe=s(["Code of Criminal Procedure Art. 233","EU Directive 2010/64/EU"],t.s)
B.b4O=new A.C("Right to Interpreter","Free interpreter at all stages. Greece transposed Directive 2010/64/EU in 2014. Availability varies by language and location. Albanian interpreters readily available; rare languages more difficult.",null)
B.bRt=s(["EU Framework Decision 2008/909/JHA","Law 4307/2014","CoE Convention ETS 112"],t.s)
B.b1B=new A.C("Transfer to Home Country","FD 2008/909/JHA implemented. Bilateral agreement with Albania (largest foreign prisoner group). CoE Convention ETS 112.",null)
B.bSP=s(["Code of Criminal Procedure Art. 340","Law 3226/2004","EU Directive 2016/1919/EU"],t.s)
B.b2w=new A.C("Legal Aid","Free legal aid for accused who cannot afford a lawyer. Mandatory for felonies. Bar association assigns counsel. Quality concerns raised by European Commission.",null)
B.c_Z=s(["Correctional Code (Law 2776/1999)","CPT reports on Greece","ECtHR judgments (multiple)"],t.s)
B.b26=new A.C("Prison Conditions","Severe overcrowding and poor conditions. ECtHR has repeatedly found violations (Art. 3 ECHR). CPT has been highly critical. Korydallos Prison in Athens particularly problematic. Conditions have slowly improved but remain below European standards.","Greek prisons are among the most overcrowded in Europe. File complaints to the supervising judge (\u03b4\u03b9\u03ba\u03b1\u03c3\u03c4\u03b9\u03ba\u03cc\u03c2 \u03bb\u03b5\u03b9\u03c4\u03bf\u03c5\u03c1\u03b3\u03cc\u03c2). Ombudsman also monitors conditions.")
B.c0d=s(["Correctional Code Art. 51-57"],t.s)
B.b3t=new A.C("Communication Rights","Visits permitted. Phone access via card-operated phones. Letters unrestricted. Lawyer visits confidential.",null)
B.c1p=s(["Correctional Code Art. 27-35"],t.s)
B.b4C=new A.C("Healthcare","Medical units in prisons. Hospital at Korydallos. Specialist referrals through public hospitals. Psychiatric care available but insufficient. CPT has criticised healthcare conditions.",null)
B.bQ5=s(["Greek Constitution Art. 13","Correctional Code Art. 37"],t.s)
B.b3H=new A.C("Religious Rights","Greek Orthodox chaplains. Muslim, Catholic services can be arranged. Religious items permitted. Halal meals available in prisons with significant Muslim populations.",null)
B.bPp=s(["Immigration Code (Law 4251/2014)","EU Directive 2004/38/EC"],t.s)
B.b2x=new A.C("Immigration Consequences","Criminal conviction typically leads to deportation order. Administrative expulsion by police. EU citizens: higher threshold. Greece is a major entry point for irregular migration, affecting prison demographics.",null)
B.bKc=s(["Criminal Code Art. 105-110"],t.s)
B.b2S=new A.C("Early Release / Parole","Conditional release after serving portion of sentence (varies by offence severity: two-fifths to four-fifths). Foreign prisoners eligible.",null)
B.bIV=s(["Immigration Code","EU Return Directive 2008/115/EC"],t.s)
B.b4V=new A.C("Deportation After Sentence","Police issue administrative expulsion. Pre-removal detention centres (often criticised for conditions). Non-refoulement applies. Deportation to Albania streamlined via bilateral agreements.",null)
B.bLT=s(["Law 3251/2004","EU Framework Decision 2002/584/JHA"],t.s)
