B.b9B=new A.ed("Austria","AT","Schulpflichtgesetz 1985, Section 1 \u2014 compulsory schooling for all children residing in Austria regardless of nationality or status",6,15,!0,"Register at the local Volksschule (primary) or nearest school. The Bildungsdirektion (Education Directorate) assigns a place. No documents strictly required for initial enrollment \u2014 schools must accept children.","Deutschf\xf6rderklassen (German Support Classes)","Since 2018/19, children scoring below threshold on MIKA-D test are placed in separate Deutschf\xf6rderklassen (up to 4 semesters, max 20 hours/week German). After that, Deutschf\xf6rderkurse (integrated support courses, 6 hrs/week).",!1,"No universal free school meals. Some municipalities (especially Vienna) offer subsidized meals. Vienna: Ganztagsschulen provide free lunch. Other L\xe4nder vary.","Equal right to Sonderp\xe4dagogischer F\xf6rderbedarf (special educational needs assessment). Inclusive education policy; children can attend regular schools with support or Sonderschulen.","Bildungsdirektion of respective Bundesland (e.g., Bildungsdirektion Wien: +43 1 52525-0)","Unaccompanied minors enrolled through Kinder- und Jugendhilfe. Asylum seeker children have full school access. Schulpflicht applies from the moment of residence, even during asylum procedure.")
B.c0x=s(["Identity document (any)","Proof of residence or declaration","Medical certificate (school doctor visit)"],t.s)
B.b9E=new A.ed("Belgium","BE","Belgian Constitution Art. 24; Compulsory Education Act 1983; Circular letters from Flemish, French, and German-speaking Communities",5,18,!0,"Contact local school directly or municipal education service. In Brussels and Wallonia, CPMS (Centre PMS) assists. In Flanders, LOP (Lokaal Overlegplatform) helps find places. Schools cannot refuse based on status.","OKAN (Onthaalklassen voor Anderstalige Nieuwkomers) in Flanders; DASPA (Dispositif d'Accueil et de Scolarisation des Primo-Arrivants) in French Community","OKAN: 1 year intensive Dutch for newcomers 6-18 years. DASPA: 1-2 years intensive French support. Both include cultural orientation. German Community has similar Auffangklassen.",!1,"No universal free meals. CPAS/OCMW social aid can cover meal costs for low-income families. Some schools in Brussels offer subsidized canteen via commune.","Equal access to buitengewoon onderwijs (special education) in Flanders or enseignement sp\xe9cialis\xe9 in Wallonia. M-decreet (Flanders) promotes inclusive education since 2015.","Flanders: Agentschap voor Onderwijsdiensten, 1700 helpline. Wallonia: Administration g\xe9n\xe9rale de l'Enseignement. Brussels: both communities.","Constitutional right \u2014 no child can be denied education. Undocumented children explicitly included. Schools penalized for refusing enrollment based on origin. Free education in public schools (small fees may apply for supplies).")
B.c_G=s(["Birth certificate or equivalent","Proof of address","Health card/vaccination record"],t.s)
B.b9H=new A.ed("Bulgaria","BG","Pre-school and School Education Act 2016 (\u0417\u0430\u043a\u043e\u043d \u0437\u0430 \u043f\u0440\u0435\u0434\u0443\u0447\u0438\u043b\u0438\u0449\u043d\u043e\u0442\u043e \u0438 \u0443\u0447\u0438\u043b\u0438\u0449\u043d\u043e\u0442\u043e \u043e\u0431\u0440\u0430\u0437\u043e\u0432\u0430\u043d\u0438\u0435), Art. 9 \u2014 right to education for all children on Bulgarian territory",7,16,!0,"Apply to the nearest school through the Regional Education Department (\u0420\u0423\u041e). Refugee children enrolled through the State Agency for Refugees (\u0414\u0410\u0411) coordination. Schools assigned by district.","\u0414\u043e\u043f\u044a\u043b\u043d\u0438\u0442\u0435\u043b\u043d\u043e \u043e\u0431\u0443\u0447\u0435\u043d\u0438\u0435 \u043f\u043e \u0431\u044a\u043b\u0433\u0430\u0440\u0441\u043a\u0438 \u0435\u0437\u0438\u043a (Additional Bulgarian Language Education)","Up to 3 additional hours per week of Bulgarian as a second language. Special preparatory groups for refugee children funded by the state. Some NGOs (Caritas, Bulgarian Red Cross) provide supplementary language support.",!0,"Free meals for grades 1-4 (primary school) since 2023 reform. Means-tested free meals for vulnerable families in higher grades. Refugee children in reception centers receive full meals.","Inclusive education guaranteed under 2016 Act. Resource teachers and support specialists provided. Special schools exist but inclusive placement preferred.","Ministry of Education and Science: +359 2 9217 799. Regional Education Departments (\u0420\u0423\u041e) in each oblast.","Asylum seekers placed in schools within 3 months of application. Unaccompanied minors assigned guardians who handle enrollment. Free textbooks for grades 1-7.")
B.bYs=s(["Any identity document","Proof of residence or reception center address","Medical certificate (available from school doctor)"],t.s)
B.b9T=new A.ed("Croatia","HR","Education Act (Zakon o odgoju i obrazovanju u osnovnoj i srednjoj \u0161koli), Art. 46; International and Temporary Protection Act",6,15,!0,"Registration through the nearest school or the Ministry of Science and Education office. Asylum seekers enrolled through coordination between the Ministry and reception centers.","Pripremna nastava hrvatskog jezika (Preparatory Croatian Language Classes)","70 hours of intensive Croatian before or during regular schooling. Available in schools with foreign-origin students. Additional support through NGOs like Are You Syrious and Croatian Red Cross.",!1,"No universal free meals. Subsidized meals through social welfare. Refugee children in reception centers receive free meals. School meal programs vary by county (\u017eupanija).","Inclusive education policy. Individual education plans (IEP) for children with special needs. Teaching assistants provided when needed.","Ministry of Science and Education: +385 1 4569 000. Education and Teacher Training Agency (AZOO).","Children granted international protection have identical rights as Croatian children. Free textbooks, transport subsidies, and extracurricular activities. Preparatory year option before mainstream enrollment.")
B.bPn=s(["Birth certificate","Proof of residence","Vaccination certificate"],t.s)
B.b9U=new A.ed("Cyprus","CY","Compulsory Education Law of 1993 (N. 24(I)/1993) and amendments; Refugee Law N. 6(I)/2000",5,15,!0,"Register at the nearest public school. District Education Office (\u0395\u03c0\u03b1\u03c1\u03c7\u03b9\u03b1\u03ba\u03cc \u0393\u03c1\u03b1\u03c6\u03b5\u03af\u03bf \u03a0\u03b1\u03b9\u03b4\u03b5\u03af\u03b1\u03c2) coordinates placement. Asylum seekers can use reception center address.","Zones of Educational Priority (ZEP) / \u0396\u03ce\u03bd\u03b5\u03c2 \u0395\u03ba\u03c0\u03b1\u03b9\u03b4\u03b5\u03c5\u03c4\u03b9\u03ba\u03ae\u03c2 \u03a0\u03c1\u03bf\u03c4\u03b5\u03c1\u03b1\u03b9\u03cc\u03c4\u03b7\u03c4\u03b1\u03c2 (\u0396\u0395\u03a0)","ZEP schools in high-immigration areas offer intensive Greek language classes. Additional afternoon Greek language courses. Teacher support staff in schools with many non-Greek-speaking students.",!1,"No universal free meals. Social Welfare Services can provide support. Some school canteens offer subsidized meals. NGOs provide lunch programs in areas with many refugee children.","Law on Special Education 113(I)/1999. Children with special needs entitled to individual support plans. Inclusive education policy applies equally to immigrants.","Ministry of Education, Sport and Youth: +357 22 800 600","All children including undocumented have school access. Greek language intensive support provided. Afternoon classes (\u0391\u03c0\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03c5\u03bc\u03b1\u03c4\u03b9\u03bd\u03ac \u03a3\u03c7\u03bf\u03bb\u03b5\u03af\u03b1) available for catch-up. Intercultural education framework in place.")
B.c1N=s(["Proof of age (any document)","Proof of residence or temporary address","Health insurance proof (recommended)"],t.s)
B.b9Q=new A.ed("Czechia","CZ","Education Act 561/2004 Sb., Section 20 \u2014 equal access for foreigners legally or illegally residing in Czechia",6,15,!0,"Apply directly to the school or through the municipal authority (obecn\xed \xfa\u0159ad). Foreign children assigned by the regional education authority. Schools must accept unless at full capacity.","Bezplatn\xe1 jazykov\xe1 p\u0159\xedprava (Free Language Preparation)","Since 2021, 200 hours of free Czech language preparation for foreign pupils in designated schools. Available for children of all foreigners with legal residence. Adaptation coordinators in schools.",!1,'No universal free meals. Subsidized lunches available. Since 2023, "Ob\u011bdy do \u0161kol" program provides free meals for socially disadvantaged children (including refugee families).',"Equal rights under inclusive education reform (2016 amendment). School counseling facilities (PPP) assess needs. Individual education plans for students with special needs.","Ministry of Education: +420 234 811 111. Czech School Inspectorate for complaints.","Ukrainian refugee children (since 2022) have special fast-track enrollment. Adaptation groups available. Free Czech courses. All foreigners including undocumented have compulsory education right.")
B.c3p=s(["CPR number (civil registration)","Proof of address"],t.s)
B.b9N=new A.ed("Denmark","DK","Folkeskolelov (Public Schools Act), Section 2 \u2014 obligation for municipalities to offer education to all children in their area",6,16,!0,"Contact the municipality (kommune). Children assigned to local folkeskole. Asylum seeker children enrolled through reception center school arrangements or local schools.","Basisundervisning i dansk som andetsprog (Basic Education in Danish as Second Language)","Modtageklasser (reception classes) for newly arrived children \u2014 up to 2 years intensive Danish. Then integration into regular classes with supplementary Danish support (supplerende dansk).",!1,"No universal free school meals in Denmark. Some municipalities run pilot programs. Packed lunches from home are the norm. Asylum center schools provide meals.","Full access to specialundervisning (special education). PPR (P\xe6dagogisk Psykologisk R\xe5dgivning) assessment available. Inclusive education principle applies.","Municipality education department. Ministry of Children and Education: +45 33 92 50 00","Asylum seeker children must be offered education within 15 working days. Unaccompanied minors receive extra support. Integration requirements for families affect continued residence but not school access.")
B.bPY=s(["Identity document or proof of age","Residence proof or accommodation center address"],t.s)
B.b9R=new A.ed("Estonia","EE","Basic Schools and Upper Secondary Schools Act (P\xf5hikooli- ja g\xfcmnaasiumiseadus), Section 9 \u2014 right to education for all children living in Estonia",7,17,!0,"Local municipality assigns school place. Apply through the local government education department or directly to schools. e-School (eKool) system used for registration.","Eesti keele kui teise keele \xf5pe (Estonian as Second Language) / LAK-\xf5pe (Language Immersion Programme)","Intensive Estonian language courses for newcomers. Language immersion program (Keelek\xfcmblus) available since 2000. Additional support hours. Some schools in Tallinn and Ida-Virumaa also offer Russian-language instruction.",!0,"Free school lunch for all students in grades 1-9 (basic education). State-funded since 2006. Upper secondary: municipality decides. All children including immigrants receive free meals.","Individual development plan (I\xd5K) for special needs. Counseling committees (Rajaleidja centers) assess needs. Inclusive education policy under 2010 reforms.","Ministry of Education and Research: +372 735 0222. Haridus- ja Noorteamet (Education and Youth Board).","Welcome program (Kohanemisprogramm) includes educational support. Asylum seeker children enrolled within days. Estonian language support starts immediately. Digital learning tools widely available.")
B.c1U=s(["No documents strictly required for enrollment"],t.s)
B.b9F=new A.ed("Finland","FI","Basic Education Act (628/1998, Perusopetuslaki) Section 4 \u2014 municipality must arrange education for all children of compulsory school age residing in the area",7,18,!0,"Contact the municipality education department (kunnan opetustoimi). Municipality assigns a nearby school. Children can enroll immediately even without residence permit \u2014 being physically present is sufficient.","Valmistava opetus (Preparatory Education)","Up to 1 year (900 hours minimum) of preparatory education before mainstream school. Finnish/Swedish as second language (S2) instruction continues in regular school. Own mother tongue teaching available (2 hrs/week). Municipalities receive extra state funding per immigrant student.",!0,"Free daily school meal for ALL students in basic education (grades 1-9) and upper secondary. Finland pioneered this in 1948. No means-testing. Includes immigrants, asylum seekers, undocumented children.","Three-tier support model: general, intensified, and special support. Equal access regardless of background. Individual education plans. Full-time special education if needed.","Finnish National Agency for Education (Opetushallitus): +358 29 533 1000. Local municipality education office.","Finland is one of the most inclusive EU countries for immigrant education. Extended compulsory education to 18 (since 2021). Free textbooks, transport, and materials in basic education. Interpreting services available. Romani and S\xe1mi language education also available.")
B.bG8=s(["Proof of age (any document)","Proof of address (or domiciliation attestation from CCAS)","Vaccination record (or catch-up arranged)"],t.s)
B.b9y=new A.ed("France","FR","Code de l'\xe9ducation Art. L131-1; Circular 2012-141 (scolarisation des \xe9l\xe8ves allophones). Constitutional principle: education is a fundamental right for all children on French territory.",3,16,!0,"Register at the mairie (town hall) which assigns a school. CASNAV (Centre Acad\xe9mique pour la Scolarisation des \xe9l\xe8ves allophones Nouvellement Arriv\xe9s et des enfants issus de familles itin\xe9rantes et de Voyageurs) evaluates language level and assigns appropriate support.","UPE2A (Unit\xe9s P\xe9dagogiques pour \xc9l\xe8ves Allophones Arrivants)","UPE2A classes provide intensive French (12-15 hrs/week) while students attend regular classes part-time. Duration: typically 1 year. CASNAV coordinates. FLE (Fran\xe7ais Langue \xc9trang\xe8re) and FLS (Fran\xe7ais Langue Seconde) methodology.",!1,"Cantine scolaire fees are income-based. Many communes offer free meals for lowest income bracket (QF). Paris: tariff 0 available. Refugee families often qualify for the lowest or zero rate.","MDPH (Maison D\xe9partementale des Personnes Handicap\xe9es) evaluates special needs. PPS (Projet Personnalis\xe9 de Scolarisation) for children with disabilities. AESH (accompaniment staff) provided. Equal rights for all children.","Rectorat of the relevant acad\xe9mie. CASNAV offices. National number: 3020 (education helpline).","Strong legal protections. Mayor CANNOT refuse enrollment based on immigration status (Conseil d'\xc9tat case law). Instruction obligation until 16, right to education until 18. Undocumented children fully protected. Free public education.")
B.bPv=s(["Proof of age","Proof of residence (Meldebescheinigung)","Vaccination record (Masern \u2014 measles mandatory since 2020)"],t.s)
B.b9M=new A.ed("Germany","DE","Grundgesetz Art. 7; each Bundesland has its own Schulgesetz with compulsory education (Schulpflicht) for all children. KMK resolution 2002: all children regardless of status.",6,18,!0,"Register at the Schulamt (school authority) or directly at the local school. Refugee children in reception facilities: enrollment organized by the Bundesland. Most L\xe4nder require enrollment within 3-6 months of arrival.","Willkommensklassen (Berlin), Vorbereitungsklassen (VKL), Deutschf\xf6rderklassen, Internationale F\xf6rderklassen (IFK) \u2014 name varies by Bundesland","Intensive German classes for 1-2 years (10-28 hrs/week depending on Land). Gradual integration into regular classes. DaZ (Deutsch als Zweitsprache) support continues. Each Land has own model \u2014 Berlin: Willkommensklassen, Bayern: Deutschklassen, NRW: Internationale F\xf6rderklassen.",!1,"No universal free meals. Bildungs- und Teilhabepaket (BuT) covers school lunch costs for families on social benefits (SGB II/XII, Asylbewerberleistungsgesetz). Ganztagsschulen provide lunch (subsidized or BuT-covered).","Sonderp\xe4dagogischer F\xf6rderbedarf assessment. Inclusive education (Inklusion) mandated since UN CRPD ratification 2009. F\xf6rderschulen available. Equal access for all children.","Schulamt of the municipality/Kreis. KMK (Kultusministerkonferenz) for federal coordination. Each Bundesland: Ministerium f\xfcr Bildung.","All 16 Bundesl\xe4nder guarantee Schulpflicht for all children. Some L\xe4nder (e.g., Hamburg) have Schulpflicht from day 1; others (e.g., Sachsen) within 3 months. Asylum-seeker children included. Unaccompanied minors get Vormundschaft + school enrollment.")
B.bMo=s(["Any age verification","Vaccination record (or catch-up at school)","AMKA or PAAYPA number (social security \u2014 can be obtained during enrollment)"],t.s)
B.b9O=new A.ed("Greece","GR","Greek Constitution Art. 16; Law 4636/2019 (International Protection Act) Art. 55; Ministerial Decision 180647/\u0393\u03944/2016",4,15,!0,"Register at the nearest school (\u03a3\u03c7\u03bf\u03bb\u03b5\u03af\u03bf). Education coordinators in refugee camps assist with enrollment. Ministry of Education assigns places through Regional Education Directorates.","\u03a4\u03ac\u03be\u03b5\u03b9\u03c2 \u03a5\u03c0\u03bf\u03b4\u03bf\u03c7\u03ae\u03c2 (Reception Classes \u2014 ZEP) / DYEP (\u0394\u03bf\u03bc\u03ad\u03c2 \u03a5\u03c0\u03bf\u03b4\u03bf\u03c7\u03ae\u03c2 \u03ba\u03b1\u03b9 \u0395\u03ba\u03c0\u03b1\u03af\u03b4\u03b5\u03c5\u03c3\u03b7\u03c2 \u03a0\u03c1\u03bf\u03c3\u03c6\u03cd\u03b3\u03c9\u03bd)","Reception classes (\u03a4\u03ac\u03be\u03b5\u03b9\u03c2 \u03a5\u03c0\u03bf\u03b4\u03bf\u03c7\u03ae\u03c2 ZEP I & II) provide intensive Greek. ZEP I: beginners. ZEP II: intermediate. DYEP: afternoon reception facilities in camps for refugee children. Frontex/UNHCR-supported language programs.",!1,"No universal free meals in Greek schools. \u03a3\u03c7\u03bf\u03bb\u03b9\u03ba\u03ac \u0393\u03b5\u03cd\u03bc\u03b1\u03c4\u03b1 (school meals program) in select disadvantaged areas since 2017. Refugee children in camps receive meals through UNHCR/NGO programs.","KEDASY (\u039a\u03ad\u03bd\u03c4\u03c1\u03b1 \u0394\u03b9\u03b5\u03c0\u03b9\u03c3\u03c4\u03b7\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03b9\u03ba\u03ae\u03c2 \u0391\u03be\u03b9\u03bf\u03bb\u03cc\u03b3\u03b7\u03c3\u03b7\u03c2) assess special needs. Law 3699/2008 on special education. Integration classes and special schools available.","Ministry of Education: +30 210 344 2000. Regional Education Directorates (\u03a0\u03b5\u03c1\u03b9\u03c6\u03b5\u03c1\u03b5\u03b9\u03b1\u03ba\u03ad\u03c2 \u0394\u03b9\u03b5\u03c5\u03b8\u03cd\u03bd\u03c3\u03b5\u03b9\u03c2 \u0395\u03ba\u03c0\u03b1\u03af\u03b4\u03b5\u03c5\u03c3\u03b7\u03c2).","Large refugee population (since 2015) led to expanded education infrastructure. Morning-zone (regular school) and afternoon-zone (DYEP) models. UNHCR and UNICEF support programs. Challenges remain in island camps. Intercultural schools in Athens, Thessaloniki.")
B.c3s=s(["Birth certificate or age proof","Address card (lakc\xedmk\xe1rtya)","TAJ card (social security) or proof of application"],t.s)
B.b9A=new A.ed("Hungary","HU","Fundamental Law Art. XI; Act CXC of 2011 on National Public Education, Section 45 \u2014 all children residing in Hungary have right and duty to attend school",3,16,!1,"Register at the district school through the Klebelsberg K\xf6zpont (education center). Refugee children enrolled through coordination with immigration authority (OIF).","Magyar nyelvi el\u0151k\xe9sz\xedt\u0151 (Hungarian Language Preparatory Classes)","Up to 1 year of Hungarian language preparation. Additional Hungarian as a foreign language support. Limited availability \u2014 concentrated in Budapest and larger cities. NGOs (Mened\xe9k, Hungarian Helsinki Committee) provide supplementary language education.",!0,"Free meals for children in grades 1-8 from families receiving social benefits. Universal free meals in kindergarten (\xf3voda). School meals heavily subsidized for all.","Expert committees (Szak\xe9rt\u0151i Bizotts\xe1gok) assess special needs. Inclusive education or special schools. Equal rights under public education act.","Klebelsberg K\xf6zpont: +36 1 795 5657. Bel\xfcgyminiszt\xe9rium (Ministry of Interior) for refugee education issues.","Refugee children have equal education rights. However, practical access can be challenging outside Budapest. Hungarian language barrier significant. Few intercultural programs. Mened\xe9k Association provides key support services.")
B.c3A=s(["Birth certificate","PPS number (can be obtained post-enrollment)","Proof of address","Immunization records"],t.s)
B.b9D=new A.ed("Ireland","IE","Education Act 1998; Education (Welfare) Act 2000; Irish Constitution Art. 42 \u2014 all children in the State entitled to education",6,16,!0,"Apply directly to schools. If refused, contact the local Educational Welfare Officer (Tusla). Schools must follow admissions policies under Education (Admission to Schools) Act 2018. Direct Provision residents have full access.","English as an Additional Language (EAL) Support","EAL support teachers in primary and post-primary schools. Up to 2 years of additional English language instruction. Post-primary: English Language Support Programme. International students can take English at a modified level in state exams.",!1,"School Meals Programme (DEIS schools) provides free meals in disadvantaged schools. Hot School Meals Programme expanding since 2023. Not universal but covers many immigrant families in DEIS schools.","EPSEN Act 2004 (Education for Persons with Special Educational Needs). NCSE (National Council for Special Education) coordinates. SNAs (Special Needs Assistants) and resource teachers provided.","Department of Education: +353 1 889 6400. Tusla Education Support Service (TESS). NCSE.","Asylum seeker children in Direct Provision have full school access. Free primary education in public schools. Post-primary: SUSI grant available for refugees. Intercultural Education Strategy in place. NALA supports adult literacy.")
B.bMk=s(["Self-declaration of personal data (autocertificazione)","Vaccination record (or catch-up)"],t.s)
B.b9V=new A.ed("Italy","IT","Italian Constitution Art. 34; D.Lgs. 286/1998 (TU Immigrazione) Art. 38 \u2014 minors present on Italian territory have right to education regardless of legal status",6,16,!0,"Register online through MIUR portal (Iscrizioni Online) or directly at school secretariat. For undocumented: self-certification accepted. Ufficio Scolastico Regionale coordinates placement.","Laboratori linguistici di italiano L2 (Italian L2 Language Workshops)","Schools organize Italian L2 laboratories (at least 2 hrs/week). Protocollo di accoglienza (welcome protocol) required in each school. Mediatori culturali (cultural mediators) in schools with many foreign students. National guidelines: C.M. 24/2006.",!1,"Mensa scolastica fees based on ISEE (income indicator). Lowest ISEE brackets: free meals. Varies by municipality. Many immigrant families qualify for free/reduced meals. Rome: fascia gratuita available.","Italy pioneered inclusive education (Legge 517/1977). Insegnante di sostegno (support teacher) for students with certified disability. 104/1992 law applies equally to all children.","Ufficio Scolastico Regionale (regional school office). MIUR helpline: 06 5849 1. Local Comune education office.","One of strongest protections in EU \u2014 Art. 38 TU Immigration explicitly states undocumented children have education rights. Schools cannot report undocumented families. Intercultural education guidelines. Cap of 30% foreign students per class (controversial, often waived).")
B.bRD=s(["Identity document","Proof of residence or asylum seeker certificate","Health certificate"],t.s)
B.b9C=new A.ed("Latvia","LV","Education Law (Izgl\u012bt\u012bbas likums) Section 3; Asylum Law Art. 28 \u2014 education rights for asylum seeker children",5,16,!0,"Apply to the municipal education department or directly to schools. Refugee children: coordinated through the Office of Citizenship and Migration Affairs (PMLP) and municipal education departments.","Latvie\u0161u valodas k\u0101 otr\u0101s valodas apguve (Latvian as Second Language)","Additional Latvian language hours in schools. Integration support program for newcomer children since 2016. Up to 480 hours of Latvian language preparation available. Bilingual education programs in some schools.",!0,"Free meals for grades 1-4 state-funded. Additional free meals for socially vulnerable children in higher grades through municipal programs. Refugee children receive free meals.","Special education commissions assess needs. Inclusive education promoted. Special schools and integrated support in mainstream schools available.","Ministry of Education and Science: +371 67 226 209. State Education Quality Service (IKVD).","Since Ukrainian refugee wave (2022), expanded integration support. Latvian language courses prioritized. Municipal coordinators for newcomer education. Free textbooks in basic education.")
B.bGz=s(["Identity document or asylum certificate","Proof of residence","Health certificate"],t.s)
B.b9J=new A.ed("Lithuania","LT","Law on Education (\u0160vietimo \u012fstatymas) Art. 24; Law on the Legal Status of Aliens Art. 28",6,16,!0,"Municipal education division assigns school. Direct application to schools possible. Refugee Registration Center coordinates for asylum seeker children.","Lietuvi\u0173 kalbos mokymasis (Lithuanian Language Learning) / Mobilios grup\u0117s (Mobile Groups)","Intensive Lithuanian language courses: up to 1 year preparatory class. Mobile groups provide language support in schools with few foreign students. 640 hours of Lithuanian language preparation funded by the state.",!0,"Free meals for socially vulnerable families. Since 2024 expansion, free meals for grades 1-4 in most municipalities. Refugee children qualify for free meals.","Pedagogical-Psychological Services (PPT) assess needs. Inclusive education policy. Special education assistants provided. Equal rights for all children.","Ministry of Education, Science and Sport: +370 5 219 1190. Education Development Center (UPC).","Expanded infrastructure since 2022 refugee arrivals. Lithuanian language support scaled up. Integration support coordinators in schools. Free textbooks and school supplies for vulnerable families.")
B.c2z=s(["Registration at commune (any proof of residence)","Birth certificate or age proof","Vaccination record"],t.s)
B.b9W=new A.ed("Luxembourg","LU","Loi du 6 f\xe9vrier 2009 on compulsory education. Constitution Art. 23. All children aged 4-16 residing in Luxembourg must attend school.",4,16,!0,"Register at the commune which assigns the school. SECAM (Service de la scolarisation des enfants \xe9trangers) evaluates linguistic competences and recommends placement.","Cours d'accueil / Alphab\xe9tisation / Classes d'insertion (CLIJA \u2014 Classes d'insertion pour jeunes adultes)","Luxembourg uses trilingual system (Luxembourgish, French, German). Cours d'accueil: intensive language classes for newcomers. CASNA (Cellule d'accueil scolaire pour \xe9l\xe8ves nouveaux arrivants) assesses and places. CLIJA classes for 12-17 year olds.",!1,"Maisons relais (after-school care) provide meals at reduced cost. Ch\xe8que-service accueil system subsidizes childcare and meals. Low-income families receive significant subsidies.","Centres de comp\xe9tences en psychop\xe9dagogie sp\xe9cialis\xe9e assess and support. Commission d'inclusion (CI) at school level. Inclusive education strengthened by 2017 law reform.","MENJE (Minist\xe8re de l'\xc9ducation nationale): +352 247-85100. CASNA: +352 247-85277.","Highly multicultural \u2014 47% of students are foreign nationals. Strong support infrastructure. SECAM/CASNA specifically for immigrant student integration. European Schools also available. Trilingual challenge significant for newcomers.")
B.bRd=s(["Birth certificate or age proof","Proof of address","eResidence card or asylum seeker document"],t.s)
B.b9I=new A.ed("Malta","MT","Education Act (Cap. 327) 1988 as amended. Refugees Act (Cap. 420). All children in Malta have right to free compulsory education.",5,16,!0,"Register at the Student Services Department within the Directorate for Educational Services. Assigned to nearest state school. Induction Hub for newcomer children assesses and prepares.","Induction Hub Programme / Complementary Education","Induction Hub: 3-6 months intensive Maltese and English for newcomer children. Bilingual system (Maltese + English). ESL (English as Second Language) support in schools. Migrant Learners Unit coordinates.",!1,"Subsidized school meals through Skolasajf program. Breakfast clubs in some schools. Social assistance covers meal costs for vulnerable families. No universal free meals.","CRPD assessment. Learning Support Educators (LSE) in schools. Inclusive Education Unit. Individual Education Programme (IEP) for students with special needs.","Directorate for Educational Services: +356 2598 2000. Migrant Learners Unit: +356 2598 2445.","Migrant Learners Unit (MLU) specifically supports immigrant education. Hubbing system for newcomers well-established. Free state education. Malta has bilingual education system \u2014 both Maltese and English used.")
B.c2o=s(["BSN number (Burgerservicenummer) \u2014 can be obtained","Proof of address","Previous school reports (if available)"],t.s)
B.b9G=new A.ed("Netherlands","NL","Leerplichtwet 1969 (Compulsory Education Act). Dutch Constitution Art. 23. All children 5-18 residing in NL must attend school.",5,18,!0,"Contact the school directly or the municipality (gemeente). Leerplichtambtenaar (compulsory education officer) ensures all children are enrolled. International Schakelklassen (ISK) for newcomers in secondary education.","ISK (Internationale Schakelklassen) / Nieuwkomersonderwijs (Newcomer Education)","ISK classes: 1-2 years intensive Dutch for secondary students (12-18). Primary: Nieuwkomersklassen or taalklassen in regular schools, up to 2 years. NT2 (Nederlands als Tweede Taal) methodology. LOWAN supports schools with newcomer education.",!1,"No universal free meals. Schoolontbijt (school breakfast) program run by charity Jeugdeducatiefonds. Since 2023, government piloting free school lunches in disadvantaged areas. Asylum center schools may provide meals.","Passend Onderwijs (Appropriate Education) since 2014. Samenwerkingsverbanden (cooperation alliances) ensure every child gets support. Equal rights for immigrant children.","DUO (Dienst Uitvoering Onderwijs): +31 50 599 9099. Gemeente education department. LOWAN (national newcomer education support).",'Strong newcomer education system. ISK well-established nationally. Undocumented children ("ongedocumenteerde kinderen") have full leerplicht and education rights (confirmed by Hoge Raad). COA (refugee agency) coordinates asylum seeker children education.')
B.bRw=s(["Any identity document","Proof of address or accommodation center address"],t.s)
B.b9P=new A.ed("Poland","PL","Prawo o\u015bwiatowe (Education Law Act) 2016, Art. 165 \u2014 foreign citizens have right to education on same terms as Polish citizens in public schools",7,18,!0,"Apply to the school designated for the residential area (szko\u0142a obwodowa). School principal enrolls the child. If needed, the Gmina (municipality) education office assists. Ukrainian refugee children have simplified fast-track enrollment.","Oddzia\u0142 przygotowawczy (Preparatory Class) / Dodatkowe zaj\u0119cia z j\u0119zyka polskiego (Additional Polish Language Classes)","Preparatory classes (oddzia\u0142 przygotowawczy): intensive Polish with core subjects, up to 12 months. Or additional Polish lessons: 2-5 hours/week for 12 months (extendable). Teacher assistant for students not speaking Polish.",!1,'Program "Posi\u0142ek w szkole i w domu" covers school meals for children from families below 150% of poverty line. Refugee families typically qualify. School canteen fees otherwise low (PLN 3-8/day).',"Poradnie psychologiczno-pedagogiczne (counseling centers) assess needs. Orzeczenie o potrzebie kszta\u0142cenia specjalnego (special education decision). Inclusive education or special schools. Equal rights for foreign children.","Kuratorium O\u015bwiaty (regional education authority) in each voivodeship. Ministry of Education: +48 22 347 41 00.","Since 2022, massive expansion for Ukrainian children (over 185,000 enrolled). Polish language support significantly expanded. Cultural assistants in schools. Free textbooks in grades 1-3. Public education entirely free.")
B.bI8=s(["Any identification (or declaration)","Proof of residence (atestado de resid\xeancia from Junta de Freguesia)"],t.s)
B.b9Y=new A.ed("Portugal","PT","Portuguese Constitution Art. 74; Lei de Bases do Sistema Educativo (Law 46/86); Decree-Law 67/2004 \u2014 all children regardless of status have right to education",6,18,!0,"Register through the school cluster (agrupamento de escolas) portal or directly at the school. PLNM (Portuguese as non-native language) assessment upon enrollment. No documents strictly required \u2014 schools must accept.","PLNM (Portugu\xeas L\xedngua N\xe3o Materna \u2014 Portuguese as Non-Native Language)","PLNM program: 3 proficiency levels (initiation, intermediate, advanced). Minimum 4 hours/week of Portuguese language support. National curriculum includes PLNM as a specific subject. Acolhimento (welcoming) teams in school clusters.",!0,"Escal\xe3o A (lowest income): free meals and school supplies. Escal\xe3o B: reduced price. ASE (A\xe7\xe3o Social Escolar) system. Refugee and immigrant families often qualify for Escal\xe3o A. Free milk and fruit programs.","Decree-Law 54/2018 on inclusive education. Universal design for learning approach. Multidisciplinary teams in schools. Equal rights for all children.","DGEstE (Dire\xe7\xe3o-Geral dos Estabelecimentos Escolares): +351 21 340 7200. ACM (Alto Comissariado para as Migra\xe7\xf5es): +351 218 106 100.","Portugal known for inclusive immigration policy. SEF replaced by AIMA (2023). ACM provides integration support. Choices Programme targets immigrant youth. No discrimination in school enrollment \u2014 Provedor de Justi\xe7a (Ombudsman) enforces.")
B.bPy=s(["Birth certificate or equivalent","Proof of address or accommodation center","Medical records"],t.s)
B.b9X=new A.ed("Romania","RO","Education Law 1/2011, Art. 45 \u2014 foreign citizens have access to education under same conditions. Constitution Art. 32.",6,16,!0,"Register at the school through Inspectoratul \u0218colar Jude\u021bean (County School Inspectorate). Refugee children: IGI (General Inspectorate for Immigration) coordinates with education authorities.","Curs de limba rom\xe2n\u0103 (Romanian Language Course) / An preg\u0103titor (Preparatory Year)","Preparatory year of intensive Romanian language (up to 1 academic year). 4-5 hours/week of additional Romanian language support. Programs delivered in schools with foreign students. NGOs (CNRR, JRS Romania) supplement language education.",!1,'Pilot "Mas\u0103 cald\u0103" (warm meal) program in disadvantaged areas expanding since 2022. Euro 200 social vouchers for school supplies (Sprijin pentru Rom\xe2nia Educat\u0103). Refugee children receive support through humanitarian programs.',"CJRAE/CMBRAE (County/Bucharest resource and assistance centers) assess special needs. Inclusive education policy. Special education support available.","Ministry of Education: +40 21 405 62 00. County School Inspectorates. CNRR (Romanian National Council for Refugees).","Growing immigrant population. Romanian language preparation available but capacity limited outside Bucharest. Free public education. Textbooks free for primary school. Ukrainian refugee children accommodated since 2022.")
B.c2v=s(["Proof of identity","Proof of residence or temporary accommodation","Health certificate"],t.s)
B.b9z=new A.ed("Slovakia","SK","School Act 245/2008 Z.z., Section 146 \u2014 children of foreigners have right to education under same conditions as Slovak citizens",6,16,!0,"Enroll at the school in the school district (\u0161kolsk\xfd obvod). Municipality assigns school. For asylum seekers: Migration Office coordinates with the Regional Education Office (Region\xe1lny \xfarad \u0161kolskej spr\xe1vy).","Jazykov\xfd kurz slovensk\xe9ho jazyka (Slovak Language Course) / Adapta\u010dn\xe9 vzdel\xe1vanie","Basic Slovak language course (up to 20 lessons/year). Adaptation education program for newcomer children. Additional Slovak as a second language support. Very limited specialized infrastructure \u2014 most support through mainstream schools.",!0,"Free school lunches for all pupils in state schools since 2023 (dot\xe1cia na stravu). Covers grades 1-9 in primary schools. One of the newest universal free meal programs in the EU.","Centres of educational-psychological counseling and prevention (CPPPaP) assess needs. Inclusive education promoted. Special schools and integration support available.","Ministry of Education: +421 2 593 74 111. Regional Education Offices (R\xda\u0160S). V\xdaDPaP (Research Institute).","Relatively small immigrant population but growing. Slovak language support capacity expanding. Free public education at all levels. School supplies support for socially disadvantaged families.")
B.bQU=s(["Proof of identity or age","Proof of residence or asylum certificate"],t.s)
B.b9S=new A.ed("Slovenia","SI","Basic School Act (Zakon o osnovni \u0161oli), Art. 10; International Protection Act. All children in Slovenia have right to compulsory education.",6,15,!0,"Register at the nearest school or through the municipal education office. Integration House (Hi\u0161a za otroke) in Ljubljana offers initial reception for newcomer children.","Za\u010detni te\u010daj sloven\u0161\u010dine (Initial Slovenian Course) / Dopolnilni pouk sloven\u0161\u010dine","Initial intensive Slovenian course: up to 1 year (120 hours). Additional supplementary Slovenian lessons (dopolnilni pouk): 2-5 hours/week during school year. Bilingual education available in areas with Italian/Hungarian minorities.",!0,"Subsidized school meals based on income bracket. Lowest income: free meals. School Nutrition Act guarantees healthy meals. Most immigrant families qualify for free or heavily subsidized meals.","Zakon o usmerjanju otrok s posebnimi potrebami (Placement of Children with Special Needs Act). Assessment by counseling services. Inclusive education model with additional support.","Ministry of Education: +386 1 400 54 00. National Education Institute of Slovenia (ZRS\u0160): +386 1 420 12 00.","Small but growing immigrant student population. Slovenian language support well-organized. Free basic education including textbooks (loan scheme). Cultural mediators available in some schools. Saturday schools for mother tongue education.")
B.bZZ=s(["Empadronamiento (municipal registration) \u2014 NO legal status required for this","Birth certificate or age proof","Vaccination record"],t.s)
B.b9K=new A.ed("Spain","ES","Spanish Constitution Art. 27; Ley Org\xe1nica 2/2006 (LOE) modified by LOMLOE 2020; Ley Org\xe1nica 4/2000 Art. 9 \u2014 all foreigners under 18 have right and duty to education",6,16,!0,"First: empadronamiento at the Ayuntamiento (free, regardless of status). Then apply to school through Comunidad Aut\xf3noma education service. Aula de enlace/acogida for initial assessment.","Aulas de Enlace (Madrid) / Aules d'Acollida (Catalonia) / Aulas ATAL (Andalusia) / Aulas de Adaptaci\xf3n Ling\xfc\xedstica \u2014 varies by Comunidad Aut\xf3noma","Intensive Spanish (or co-official language) classes for newcomers. Typically 6-12 months. Aulas de enlace (Madrid): full-time intensive for 6-9 months. ATAL (Andalusia): itinerant teachers visit schools. Catalonia: Aules d'acollida + Pla educatiu d'entorn.",!1,"Becas de comedor (meal grants) available through Comunidades Aut\xf3nomas. Income-based. Many immigrant families qualify. Andaluc\xeda, Valencia: extensive free meal programs for vulnerable families. Each region has own system.","Equipos de Orientaci\xf3n Educativa y Psicopedag\xf3gica (EOEP) assess needs. Inclusive education under LOMLOE. Adaptaciones curriculares (curriculum adaptations). Equal rights for all children.","Ministerio de Educaci\xf3n: 910 837 937. Regional Consejer\xedas de Educaci\xf3n. Defensor del Pueblo for complaints.","Very strong protections. Empadronamiento (not residence permit) is the key document \u2014 available to ALL including undocumented. After empadronamiento, full access to education, health, social services. 17 Comunidades Aut\xf3nomas each have own programs.")
B.bUV=s(["No documents strictly required"],t.s)
B.b9L=new A.ed("Sweden","SE","Skollag (Education Act) 2010:800, Chapter 29 Section 2 \u2014 all children in Sweden have right to education. Includes asylum seekers and undocumented (pappersl\xf6sa) children.",6,16,!0,"Municipality (kommun) is obligated to offer school place. Contact the kommun education office (utbildningsf\xf6rvaltningen). Assignment within 1 month of arrival. Asylum seekers: Migrationsverket coordinates with kommun.","F\xf6rberedelseklass (Preparatory Class) / Studiehandledning p\xe5 modersm\xe5let (Study Guidance in Mother Tongue)","F\xf6rberedelseklass: intensive Swedish for newcomers (individualized duration). SVA (Svenska som andraspr\xe5k \u2014 Swedish as Second Language): throughout schooling. Modersm\xe5lsundervisning (mother tongue education): if 5+ students speak same language. Studiehandledning: subjects explained in child's language.",!0,"Free school lunch for ALL students in grundskola (compulsory school) and often in gymnasieskola (upper secondary). Universal \u2014 no means-testing. Sweden pioneered this alongside Finland. All children including undocumented receive free meals.","Skollag Chapter 3: all students entitled to support. Extra anpassningar (additional adjustments) and s\xe4rskilt st\xf6d (special support). \xc5tg\xe4rdsprogram (action plan) for students needing help. Specialpedagog/speciall\xe4rare in schools.","Skolverket (National Agency for Education): +46 8 527 332 00. Municipal education office (Utbildningsf\xf6rvaltning). Skolinspektionen (School Inspectorate) for complaints.",'Since 2013 law change, even "pappersl\xf6sa" (undocumented) children have RIGHT (not just access) to education. One of strongest protections in EU. Kartl\xe4ggning (mapping) of prior knowledge on arrival. Extensive mother tongue support system. Newly arrived students exempt from certain grading initially.')
