B.ako=new A.eP("Public schools must accommodate dietary needs upon parental request. Many schools in Vienna, Graz offer halal meals as standard option.","Widely available in Vienna, Graz, Linz. Halal certification by IGG\xd6 (Islamic Religious Authority in Austria).")
B.b8A=new A.f0("Muslims entitled to leave on Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha under Islamgesetz 2015. Jewish employees entitled to Yom Kippur, Rosh Hashanah. Must agree with employer; unpaid unless otherwise negotiated.")
B.b8g=new A.eZ("Generally permitted in private sector. Employers may restrict for safety/hygiene reasons only with proportional justification.","Anti-Face-Covering Act (Anti-Gesichtsverh\xfcllungsgesetz) 2017 bans full face coverings in public spaces. Fine: \u20ac150.")
B.b0T=new A.eY("No legal obligation. Many large employers (e.g., \xd6BB, Siemens Austria) voluntarily provide multi-faith prayer rooms.")
B.bE5=new A.f_()
B.bDp=new A.eX()
B.a84=new A.eJ(u.hv,"Taubstummengasse 11, 1040 Vienna. Tel: +43 1 53220")
B.TY=new A.eB("Islamic burial sections in Vienna (Zentralfriedhof Group 27A, Liesing Islamic Cemetery), Graz, Linz, Innsbruck. Burial without coffin permitted in dedicated sections. 24-hour burial not guaranteed but expedited.")
B.bzg=new A.eE()
B.b8M=new A.ec("Austria","AT","Basic Law on the General Rights of Nationals (1867) Art 14-16; Islamgesetz 2015 (Islam Act); Israelitengesetz 2012; Equal Treatment Act (Gleichbehandlungsgesetz) 2004.","Art 14 StGG guarantees full freedom of conscience and religion. Art 15 grants recognized religious communities corporate status. Islam has been officially recognized since 1912 (oldest recognition in Western Europe).",B.ako,B.b8A,B.b8g,B.b0T,B.a84,B.TY,"Austria officially recognizes Islam since 1912 \u2014 the oldest recognition in Western Europe. Islamgesetz 2015 updated the framework but also banned foreign funding of mosques. Immigrants from Muslim-majority countries benefit from well-established IGG\xd6 infrastructure. Anti-face-covering law and under-10 headscarf ban are points of contention. Integration Agreement (Integrationsvereinbarung) requires language/values courses but does not restrict religious practice.")
B.akj=new A.eP("Varies by region. Flanders: many schools offer halal options. Wallonia/Brussels: halal meals increasingly standard in schools with significant Muslim populations.","Widely available, especially in Brussels, Antwerp, Li\xe8ge. Strong halal food industry with Belgian certification bodies.")
B.b8J=new A.f0("Employees may request leave for religious holidays using annual leave or through collective agreement. No statutory right to specific non-Christian holidays. Some CBAs in Brussels include Eid provisions.")
B.b8h=new A.eZ("Private sector: employers may impose dress code if applied neutrally. Belgian Court of Cassation (2020) upheld employer neutrality policies.","Full face covering ban since 2011 (Law of 1 June 2011). Fine: \u20ac15-\u20ac25 and/or up to 7 days imprisonment. Upheld by ECHR in Belcacemi and Oussar v. Belgium (2017).")
B.b0X=new A.eY("No legal obligation. Larger employers (BNP Paribas Fortis, Proximus) sometimes provide quiet rooms.")
B.bE6=new A.f_()
B.bDq=new A.eX()
B.a8c=new A.eJ(u.ea,"Rue Royale 138, 1000 Brussels. Tel: +32 2 212 30 00. Free helpline: 0800 12 800")
B.Ul=new A.eB("Islamic burial sections exist in Brussels (Schaerbeek cemetery), Antwerp, Li\xe8ge, Charleroi. Burial without coffin permitted in some communes. Mecca-facing orientation accommodated in dedicated sections.")
B.bzh=new A.eE()
B.b91=new A.ec("Belgium","BE","Constitution Art 19-21 (freedom of worship); Law of 4 March 1870 (temporal aspects of worship); Anti-Discrimination Law 2007 (Loi anti-discrimination); EU Directive 2000/78 transposed.","Art 19: Freedom of worship guaranteed. Art 20: No one can be compelled to participate in religious acts. Art 21: State may not interfere in appointment of ministers of religion. Six recognized religions: Catholicism, Protestantism, Anglicanism, Judaism, Islam (since 1974), Orthodox Christianity.",B.akj,B.b8J,B.b8h,B.b0X,B.a8c,B.Ul,"Belgium recognized Islam in 1974 but the institutional framework (EMB) has been repeatedly restructured. Ritual slaughter bans in Flanders and Wallonia significantly affect Muslim and Jewish communities \u2014 Brussels remains the exception. Strong anti-discrimination framework through Unia. Significant Muslim population (~7% of total) means services are relatively well-developed in major cities. Achbita CJEU case originated in Belgium and shapes EU-wide headscarf jurisprudence.")
B.aky=new A.eP("No systematic provision. Parents may send packed meals. Some schools in areas with Turkish/Muslim minorities (Kardzhali, Razgrad) provide pork-free options.","Halal food available in areas with Muslim population (northeastern Bulgaria, Rhodope region). Limited in Sofia.")
B.b8v=new A.f0("Art 173 Labour Code allows use of annual leave for religious holidays. No specific statutory right to non-Orthodox holidays.")
B.b7X=new A.eZ("No specific legislation. Generally permitted unless employer has justified safety requirements.","Full face covering ban enacted 2016 (Amendment to the law on limiting the wearing of clothing concealing the face). Fine: BGN 200 (first offense) to BGN 1,500 (repeat).")
B.b10=new A.eY("No legal obligation.")
B.bE7=new A.f_()
B.bDr=new A.eX()
B.a8m=new A.eJ("Commission for Protection Against Discrimination (\u041a\u043e\u043c\u0438\u0441\u0438\u044f \u0437\u0430 \u0437\u0430\u0449\u0438\u0442\u0430 \u043e\u0442 \u0434\u0438\u0441\u043a\u0440\u0438\u043c\u0438\u043d\u0430\u0446\u0438\u044f)","Ul. Dragan Tsankov 35, 1797 Sofia. Tel: +359 2 807 3030")
B.U7=new A.eB("Muslim cemeteries exist in areas with Muslim populations. Chief Muftiate manages Islamic burial grounds. Shroud burial (without coffin) practiced in traditional Muslim areas.")
B.bzi=new A.eE()
B.b8Z=new A.ec("Bulgaria","BG","Constitution Art 13, 37 (freedom of conscience and religion); Religious Denominations Act 2002 (\u0417\u0430\u043a\u043e\u043d \u0437\u0430 \u0432\u0435\u0440\u043e\u0438\u0437\u043f\u043e\u0432\u0435\u0434\u0430\u043d\u0438\u044f\u0442\u0430); Protection Against Discrimination Act 2003.",'Art 13: Freedom of religion is inviolable. Eastern Orthodox Christianity is the "traditional religion." Art 37: Freedom of conscience, thought, and religion; right to perform rites.',B.aky,B.b8v,B.b7X,B.b10,B.a8m,B.U7,"Bulgaria has a historic Muslim minority (~12% of population, mainly ethnic Turks and Pomaks) with established infrastructure. Immigrants from other Muslim countries may find less developed services. The Chief Muftiate is the official Islamic representative body. Face covering ban enacted 2016. ECHR has ruled against Bulgaria for state interference in Muslim community leadership.")
B.akG=new A.eP("No systematic halal/kosher provision. Schools generally offer meat-free alternatives.","Limited halal options. Available in Zagreb through specialized shops. Islamic Community of Croatia provides guidance.")
B.b8o=new A.f0("Employees may use annual leave for religious holidays. Agreement with Islamic Community provides for Eid recognition.")
B.b8j=new A.eZ("No specific legislation. Generally permitted. Anti-Discrimination Act protects against religious discrimination in employment.","No face covering ban.")
B.b11=new A.eY("No legal obligation.")
B.bEi=new A.f_()
B.bDC=new A.eX()
B.a8n=new A.eJ("Ombudsman (Pu\u010dki pravobranitelj) and specialized offices","Savska cesta 41/3, 10000 Zagreb. Tel: +385 1 4851 855")
B.Uj=new A.eB("Islamic cemetery section in Zagreb (Mirogoj). Islamic Community manages burial according to Islamic rites.")
B.bzt=new A.eE()
B.b8O=new A.ec("Croatia","HR","Constitution Art 40-41 (freedom of conscience and religion); Legal Status of Religious Communities Act 2002 (Zakon o pravnom polo\u017eaju vjerskih zajednica); Anti-Discrimination Act 2008.","Art 40: Freedom of conscience and religion. Art 41: Religious communities equal before law, separated from state. Concordat with Holy See (1996-1998). Agreements with 19 other religious communities including Islamic Community.",B.akG,B.b8o,B.b8j,B.b11,B.a8n,B.Uj,"Croatia has a small but established Muslim community (mainly Bosniaks). Islamic Community of Croatia (Islamska zajednica u Hrvatskoj) is the official body. Religious freedom generally respected but infrastructure for non-Christian religions is limited. No face-covering ban. Anti-Discrimination Act provides protection. Country is a newer EU member (2013) still developing immigrant integration services.")
B.aks=new A.eP("Limited formal provision. Some schools accommodate upon request.","Halal food available in Larnaca, Limassol (areas with larger Muslim populations from immigration). Growing availability.")
B.b8z=new A.f0("Employees may use annual leave for non-Orthodox religious holidays.")
B.b81=new A.eZ(u.oO,"No face covering ban.")
B.b12=new A.eY("No legal obligation.")
B.bEp=new A.f_()
B.bDJ=new A.eX()
B.a8a=new A.eJ("Commissioner for Administration and Human Rights (Ombudsman) / Equality Authority","Era House, Diagorou 4, 1097 Nicosia. Tel: +357 22 405500")
B.U2=new A.eB("Muslim cemeteries exist in Larnaca and Limassol. Turkish Cypriot communities maintain cemeteries.")
B.bzA=new A.eE()
B.b95=new A.ec("Cyprus","CY","Constitution Art 18 (freedom of religion); Law on Religious Groups 1960; Equal Treatment in Employment Law 2004 (transposing Directive 2000/78/EC).","Art 18: Every person has the right to freedom of thought, conscience and religion. Three religious groups constitutionally recognized: Maronites, Armenian-Apostolic, Latin (Roman Catholic). Islam recognized through Turkish Cypriot community provisions.",B.aks,B.b8z,B.b81,B.b12,B.a8a,B.U2,"Cyprus has a unique religious landscape due to the division. Republic of Cyprus (Greek Cypriot) is predominantly Orthodox. Growing immigrant Muslim population (from South/Southeast Asia, Middle East, Africa). Infrastructure for Muslim immigrants is limited. No burqa ban. Generally tolerant but services for non-Orthodox religions are underdeveloped.")
B.akD=new A.eP("No systematic provision. Very low demand. Some Prague schools accommodate individual requests.","Very limited. Prague has some halal restaurants and shops (around Karl\xedn). Kosher options through Jewish Community of Prague.")
B.b8k=new A.f0("Employees use annual leave or unpaid leave for religious holidays. Employer should consider reasonable accommodation.")
B.b8_=new A.eZ("No specific legislation. Generally permitted.","No face covering ban despite political proposals.")
B.b18=new A.eY("No legal obligation.")
B.bEq=new A.f_()
B.bDK=new A.eX()
B.a8h=new A.eJ("Public Defender of Rights (Ve\u0159ejn\xfd ochr\xe1nce pr\xe1v / Ombudsman)","\xdadoln\xed 39, 602 00 Brno. Tel: +420 542 542 888")
B.Ud=new A.eB("Very limited. No dedicated Islamic cemeteries. Some cemeteries in Prague accommodate Muslim burial practices.")
B.bzB=new A.eE()
B.b8N=new A.ec("Czech Republic","CZ","Charter of Fundamental Rights and Freedoms Art 15-16 (constitutional law); Act on Churches and Religious Societies 2002 (3/2002 Sb.); Anti-Discrimination Act 2009 (198/2009 Sb.).","Art 15: Freedom of thought, conscience, religion. Art 16: Right to profess faith publicly or privately. Czech Republic is one of the most secular countries in Europe. 42 registered churches/religious societies.",B.akD,B.b8k,B.b8_,B.b18,B.a8h,B.Ud,"Czech Republic is one of the most secular and skeptical-of-Islam countries in the EU. Very small Muslim population (~20,000). Infrastructure for Islamic practice is minimal. No face covering ban despite political pressure. Ritual slaughter banned \u2014 halal/kosher meat must be imported. Islamic Foundation registered since 2004. Generally tolerant legal framework but public attitudes can be unwelcoming. Anti-Discrimination Act provides basic protection.")
B.akr=new A.eP("Municipalities decide. Many schools in Copenhagen, Aarhus offer halal or pork-free options.","Widely available in Copenhagen, Aarhus, Odense. Well-established halal food industry.")
B.b8K=new A.f0("Employees may negotiate leave for religious holidays. Use annual leave or unpaid leave. Some collective agreements include provisions.")
B.b7V=new A.eZ("Permitted unless employer demonstrates objective justification for restrictions. Board of Equal Treatment has ruled on multiple headscarf cases.",'Face covering ban enacted 2018 ("Burka ban"). Fine: DKK 1,000 (first offense) to DKK 10,000 (fourth offense).')
B.b0R=new A.eY("No legal obligation. Some employers provide quiet rooms.")
B.bEr=new A.f_()
B.bDL=new A.eX()
B.a82=new A.eJ("Board of Equal Treatment (Ligebehandlingsn\xe6vnet)","N\xe6vnenes Hus, Toldboden 2, 8800 Viborg. Tel: +45 72 40 50 00")
B.U0=new A.eB("Islamic burial sections in Copenhagen (Br\xf8ndby Muslim Cemetery, opened 2006 \u2014 Denmark's first purpose-built). Sections in Aarhus, Odense.")
B.bzC=new A.eE()
B.b8W=new A.ec("Denmark","DK","Constitution \xa767-70 (freedom of religion); Act on Equal Treatment 1996; Anti-Discrimination Act. Evangelical Lutheran Church is state church (\xa74 Constitution).",'\xa767: Citizens have right to worship God according to conviction. \xa770: No deprivation of civic rights due to faith. Evangelical Lutheran Church supported by state (\xa74). Other religions are "approved" (godkendte) or "recognized."',B.akr,B.b8K,B.b7V,B.b0R,B.a82,B.U0,"Denmark has one of Europe's strictest immigration policies but protects religious freedom constitutionally. Face covering ban since 2018. Ritual slaughter without stunning banned since 2014. Islamic free schools under increased scrutiny \u2014 several closed for alleged anti-democratic values. Br\xf8ndby Muslim Cemetery was a landmark achievement. Political climate can be challenging for Muslim immigrants but legal protections through Board of Equal Treatment are solid.")
B.akB=new A.eP("No formal provision. Very limited demand.","Very limited. Some halal options in Tallinn. Small Muslim community (~2,000-5,000).")
B.b8C=new A.f0(u.aW)
B.b84=new A.eZ("No specific restrictions. Equal Treatment Act covers religious discrimination.","No face covering ban.")
B.b19=new A.eY("No legal obligation.")
B.bEs=new A.f_()
B.bDM=new A.eX()
B.a8k=new A.eJ("Gender Equality and Equal Treatment Commissioner (Soolise v\xf5rd\xf5iguslikkuse ja v\xf5rdse kohtlemise volinik)","Roosikrantsi 8b, 10119 Tallinn. Tel: +372 626 9259")
B.Ub=new A.eB("Very limited. Small section in Tallinn cemeteries. Muslim community arranges burial individually.")
B.bzD=new A.eE()
B.b8X=new A.ec("Estonia","EE","Constitution \xa740-41 (freedom of religion); Churches and Congregations Act 2002; Equal Treatment Act 2008.","\xa740: Everyone has freedom of conscience, religion, and thought. \xa741: Right to remain faithful to opinions and convictions. No state church. One of most secular countries in Europe.",B.akB,B.b8C,B.b84,B.b19,B.a8k,B.Ub,"Estonia is one of Europe's most secular countries with a very small Muslim population. Infrastructure for Islamic practice is minimal. No face covering ban, no specific restrictions on religious clothing. Legal framework provides basic protection against discrimination. Estonian Islamic Centre in Tallinn is the primary institution. Ritual slaughter without stunning is banned.")
B.akz=new A.eP("Schools must accommodate special diets including religious diets under Basic Education Act. Helsinki, Espoo, Vantaa, Turku, Tampere regularly provide halal options in school meals.","Available in Helsinki, Espoo, Turku, Tampere. Growing halal food industry. Finnish Islamic Council provides guidance.")
B.b8n=new A.f0("Employees may negotiate leave for religious holidays. Annual leave or unpaid leave used. Non-Discrimination Act requires reasonable accommodation. Non-Discrimination Ombudsman has emphasized employer flexibility.")
B.b8d=new A.eZ("Generally permitted. Non-Discrimination Act 2014 protects against religious discrimination. Employer restrictions must be proportionate and based on genuine occupational requirements.","No face covering ban. Proposed in 2018 parliament but not enacted.")
B.b0V=new A.eY("No legal obligation but Non-Discrimination Act encourages reasonable accommodation. Many larger employers provide quiet rooms.")
B.bEt=new A.f_()
B.bDN=new A.eX()
B.a86=new A.eJ("Non-Discrimination Ombudsman (Yhdenvertaisuusvaltuutettu)","P.O. Box 24, 00023 Government, Helsinki. Tel: +358 295 666 817")
B.TX=new A.eB("Islamic burial section in Helsinki (Honkanummi cemetery, opened 2012). Sections in Turku and Tampere. Burial in shroud (without coffin) permitted in designated sections. Mecca-facing orientation accommodated.")
B.bzE=new A.eE()
B.b8T=new A.ec("Finland","FI","Constitution \xa711 (freedom of religion and conscience); Freedom of Religion Act 2003 (453/2003); Non-Discrimination Act 2014 (1325/2014); Act on the Evangelical Lutheran Church; Act on the Orthodox Church.","\xa711: Freedom of religion and conscience includes the right to profess and practice a religion, to express convictions, and to belong or not to a religious community. Two national churches: Evangelical Lutheran and Orthodox.",B.akz,B.b8n,B.b8d,B.b0V,B.a86,B.TX,"Finland has a growing Muslim population (~100,000-120,000, ~2% of population). Strong legal framework through Non-Discrimination Act 2014 and Freedom of Religion Act 2003. No face covering ban. Ritual slaughter without stunning banned but imported meat permitted. School meal accommodation is legally required. Islamic religious education available in major cities. Honkanummi Islamic cemetery section was a significant development. Finnish Islamic Council (FISU) is key representative body. Integration services support religious practice. Non-Discrimination Ombudsman actively handles religious discrimination cases.")
B.akq=new A.eP("Public schools generally offer alternative menus (without pork) but no obligation to provide certified halal or kosher meals. Varies by municipality. Some cities removed pork-free options (political controversy).","France has Europe's largest halal market. Widely available nationwide. Major certification bodies: AVS, ARGML, Mosqu\xe9e de Paris.")
B.b8m=new A.f0("Employees may request absence for religious holidays. Employer should accommodate unless operational necessity prevents it. Cour de cassation: refusal must be objectively justified.")
B.b8f=new A.eZ("Private sector: employer can restrict if justified by genuine occupational requirement or documented in internal regulations (r\xe8glement int\xe9rieur). Cour de cassation Baby Loup case (2014): employer neutrality upheld.","Law of 11 October 2010: full face covering banned in public spaces (niqab/burqa). Fine: \u20ac150. Upheld by ECHR in S.A.S. v. France (2014).")
B.b0Z=new A.eY("No obligation under la\xefcit\xe9. Employer may provide but not required. Some companies provide multi-faith rooms voluntarily.")
B.bEu=new A.f_()
B.bDO=new A.eX()
B.a8q=new A.eJ(u.iB,"TSA 90716, 75334 Paris Cedex 07. Tel: +33 9 69 39 00 00")
B.Uc=new A.eB("Square musulman (Muslim sections) in municipal cemeteries. Circular of 19 February 2008 encourages mayors to create Muslim sections. Available in most major cities. Burial without coffin: varies by commune \u2014 some allow shroud burial in dedicated sections.")
B.bzF=new A.eE()
B.b8L=new A.ec("France","FR",'Constitution Art 1 (la\xefcit\xe9); Law of 9 December 1905 (Separation of Churches and State); Law of 24 August 2021 (Loi confortant le respect des principes de la R\xe9publique \u2014 "Separatism Law"); Penal Code Art 225-1 (discrimination).',"Art 1: France is an indivisible, secular (la\xefque) Republic. It ensures equality before the law regardless of religion. It respects all beliefs. La\xefcit\xe9 is a constitutional principle \u2014 strict separation of state and religion.",B.akq,B.b8m,B.b8f,B.b0Z,B.a8q,B.Uc,"France has the largest Muslim population in Western Europe (~5-6 million, ~8-9%). La\xefcit\xe9 creates a unique framework \u2014 religion is strictly private matter. School headscarf ban since 2004 and face covering ban since 2010 are the most restrictive in the EU. However, halal slaughter exemption maintained, prison/military chaplaincy funded by state, and private religious schools including Islamic ones receive state funding. Loi s\xe9paratisme (2021) increased scrutiny of Islamic organizations. D\xe9fenseur des droits actively handles discrimination. Strong legal aid network. Immigrant religious practice is constitutionally protected but public expression is more restricted than in most EU countries.")
B.akx=new A.eP("Varies by Land (state). Many schools in Berlin, NRW, Hamburg, Hessen offer halal meals. No federal mandate.","Widely available throughout Germany. Strong halal food industry. Large Turkish/Muslim population ensures broad availability.")
B.b8u=new A.f0("AGG requires equal treatment. Employees may take annual leave for religious holidays. Some collective agreements (Tarifvertr\xe4ge) include provisions. Employer should consider reasonable accommodation under Art 4 GG.")
B.b8a=new A.eZ("Generally permitted under Art 4 GG. AGG protects against religious discrimination. BAG (Federal Labour Court) has addressed headscarf in employment repeatedly.","No general face covering ban. Partial restrictions: Hessen, Bavaria, Lower Saxony ban in some public sector contexts. No federal burqa ban.")
B.b1_=new A.eY("No statutory obligation. Art 4 GG may require reasonable accommodation in some circumstances. BAG has not mandated prayer rooms.")
B.bEv=new A.f_()
B.bDP=new A.eX()
B.a87=new A.eJ("Federal Anti-Discrimination Agency (Antidiskriminierungsstelle des Bundes \u2014 ADS)","Glinkastra\xdfe 24, 10117 Berlin. Tel: +49 30 18555 1855")
B.Uf=new A.eB("Islamic sections in most major city cemeteries. Sargpflicht (coffin requirement) varies by Land \u2014 NRW, Bremen abolished it. Berlin allows shroud burial in designated areas. Eternal rest (no grave reuse): some L\xe4nder accommodate.")
B.bzG=new A.eE()
B.b92=new A.ec("Germany","DE","Basic Law (Grundgesetz) Art 4 (freedom of faith/conscience), Art 3 (non-discrimination), Art 140 (Weimar Constitution religion articles); General Equal Treatment Act 2006 (AGG \u2014 Allgemeines Gleichbehandlungsgesetz).","Art 4 GG: Inviolability of freedom of faith, conscience, and religious/philosophical creed. Undisturbed practice of religion guaranteed. Art 140 incorporates Weimar Constitution articles on religion \u2014 cooperative model between state and religious communities (K\xf6rperschaft des \xf6ffentlichen Rechts status).",B.akx,B.b8u,B.b8a,B.b1_,B.a87,B.Uf,"Germany has ~5.5 million Muslims (~6.5% of population), mostly Turkish-origin. Strong constitutional protection under Art 4 GG. Federal Constitutional Court has been protective of religious freedom (headscarf rulings, slaughter exemptions). Islamic RE being rolled out across L\xe4nder. No federal face covering ban. AGG provides anti-discrimination framework. Deutsche Islam Konferenz established 2006 for structured dialogue. DITIB is largest Islamic organization but faces scrutiny over Turkish government ties. Islamic theology chairs at five universities training imams and chaplains. Coffin requirement being relaxed in multiple L\xe4nder for Islamic burial.")
B.akw=new A.eP("Muslim schools in Western Thrace provide halal meals. No systematic provision elsewhere.","Available in Athens (Metaxourgeio area, central market), Thessaloniki, and extensively in Western Thrace (Komotini, Xanthi).")
B.b8x=new A.f0("Employees may use annual leave. No statutory non-Orthodox holiday rights.")
B.b82=new A.eZ(u.oO,"No face covering ban.")
B.b1a=new A.eY("No legal obligation.")
B.bE8=new A.f_()
B.bDs=new A.eX()
B.a8g=new A.eJ("Greek Ombudsman (\u03a3\u03c5\u03bd\u03ae\u03b3\u03bf\u03c1\u03bf\u03c2 \u03c4\u03bf\u03c5 \u03a0\u03bf\u03bb\u03af\u03c4\u03b7)","Chalkokondyli 17, 10432 Athens. Tel: +30 213 1306 600")
B.U4=new A.eB("Muslim cemeteries in Western Thrace (Komotini, Xanthi, Alexandroupoli). Athens: Muslim section in Schisto cemetery. Limited availability.")
B.bzj=new A.eE()
B.b99=new A.ec("Greece","GR","Constitution Art 13 (religious freedom), Art 3 (prevailing religion); Law 4301/2014 (organization of religious communities); Law 4356/2015 (anti-discrimination). Treaty of Lausanne 1923 (Muslim minority in Thrace).",'Art 3: Eastern Orthodox Church is the "prevailing religion." Art 13: Freedom of religious conscience inviolable. Proselytism prohibited. Known and recognized religions enjoy protection.',B.akw,B.b8x,B.b82,B.b1a,B.a8g,B.U4,'Greece has a constitutionally established Muslim minority in Western Thrace (~120,000, under Treaty of Lausanne 1923) with mosques, schools, muftis. Immigrant Muslims (~500,000+) outside Thrace have much less infrastructure. Athens Mosque opened 2020 after decades of delay \u2014 major milestone. No face covering ban. Orthodox Church constitutionally "prevailing" creates asymmetry. Proselytism prohibition technically still in law. ECHR has ruled against Greece on several religious freedom matters. Mufti appointment controversy in Thrace ongoing.')
