B.b9_=new A.ec("Ireland","IE","Constitution (Bunreacht na h\xc9ireann) Art 44 (religion); Employment Equality Acts 1998-2015; Equal Status Acts 2000-2018; Irish Human Rights and Equality Commission Act 2014.",'Art 44: State acknowledges homage to Almighty God. Freedom of conscience and free profession and practice of religion guaranteed. State shall not endow any religion. All religions treated equally (post-1972 amendment removing "special position" of Catholic Church).',B.akv,B.b8p,B.b7W,B.b0Y,B.a8b,B.U5,"Ireland has a growing and increasingly diverse Muslim community (~85,000). Generally welcoming legal environment with no face covering ban, no headscarf restrictions, and ritual slaughter permitted. The denominational school system is the main challenge \u2014 90% Catholic patronage means limited non-Catholic options, though Educate Together and Muslim schools are expanding. Education admission reform (2018) removed baptism barrier. Strong equality legislation. Islamic Cultural Centre of Ireland (Clonskeagh) is a major community resource.")
B.akm=new A.eP("Varies by municipality. Milan, Rome, Turin schools increasingly offer halal/kosher options. No national mandate.","Widely available, especially in Rome, Milan, Turin, Bologna. Large Muslim population ensures market demand.")
B.b8w=new A.f0("Employees of religious communities with intesa have specific rights. Muslims without intesa rely on annual leave and employer goodwill.")
B.b80=new A.eZ("No specific restrictions. Anti-discrimination decree applies.","No specific burqa/niqab ban but Law 152/1975 and TULPS Art 85 prohibit covering face in public places for identification purposes. Applied to niqab by some local ordinances and police. Fines vary.")
