B.b94=new A.ec("Latvia","LV","Constitution (Satversme) Art 99 (freedom of religion); Law on Religious Organizations 1995; Labour Law Art 29 (discrimination prohibition).","Art 99: Freedom of thought, conscience and religion. Church and state separated. Traditional religious denominations recognized: Lutheran, Catholic, Orthodox, Old Believers, Baptist, Methodist, Adventist, Jewish.",B.akC,B.b8E,B.b7Z,B.b1d,B.a88,B.U8,"Latvia has a very small Muslim population (~1,000-2,000). Minimal Islamic infrastructure. No mosques. Islamic Cultural Centre in Riga is primary institution. No face covering ban. Legal framework provides basic anti-discrimination protection. Religious freedom constitutionally guaranteed but practical accommodation for Muslim immigrants is minimal.")
