B.b8V=new A.ec("Slovakia","SK","Constitution Art 24 (freedom of religion); Act 308/1991 on Freedom of Religious Faith; Anti-Discrimination Act 365/2004.","Art 24: Freedom of thought, conscience, religion and faith guaranteed. Right to change religion. Right to manifest religion publicly or privately. Registration requires 50,000 adult members (since 2017 amendment \u2014 highest threshold in EU).",B.akg,B.b8F,B.b7Y,B.b16,B.a8s,B.Ug,"Slovakia has the highest registration threshold in the EU (50,000 members), which effectively prevents the Islamic community from registering. This means no state funding, limited institutional access, and reduced rights compared to registered religions. Very small Muslim population (~5,000). No mosques. Islamic Foundation in Bratislava operates from rented premises. No face covering ban. Anti-Discrimination Act provides basic protection. One of the most challenging EU countries for Muslim religious practice.")
B.akp=new A.eP("Some accommodation in Ljubljana schools.","Limited. Ljubljana has some halal options. Muslim community (~50,000, mainly Bosniak).")
