B.auo=new A.ds("France","FR",B.cC,'Same-sex marriage legal since May 18, 2013 (Loi n\xb0 2013-404, "Marriage pour tous"). PACS (Pacte civil de solidarit\xe9) available since 1999. Concubinage (cohabitation) also recognized.',!0,"Apply at SPADA (structure de premier accueil des demandeurs d'asile) then GUDA (guichet unique). OFPRA (Office fran\xe7ais de protection des r\xe9fugi\xe9s et apatrides) processes claims. SOGI-trained officers. Appeal to CNDA (Cour nationale du droit d'asile).","ARDHIS (Association pour la Reconnaissance des Droits des Personnes Homosexuelles et Transsexuelles \xe0 l'Immigration et au S\xe9jour), ORAM France, Cimade, France Terre d'Asile.",!0,B.ds,B.hg,"Generally safe, especially in Paris, Lyon, and other major cities. Le Marais (Paris) is a historic LGBTQ+ district. French Riviera also very accepting. Some violence incidents reported, particularly in certain suburbs. SOS Homophobie monitors incidents.",67,"Foreign same-sex marriages fully recognized. PACS available to foreign nationals. Family reunification for same-sex spouses. Titre de s\xe9jour vie priv\xe9e et familiale for partners. AME (Aide M\xe9dicale de l'\xc9tat) covers undocumented persons' healthcare.","France has extensive SOGI asylum experience. ARDHIS is the key specialized organization. OFPRA has SOGI-trained units. Accommodation system (CADA, HUDA) sometimes problematic for LGBTQ+ persons - request specific placement. Paris has the most resources but Lyon, Marseille, Lille also have support.")
