B.auM=new A.ds("Germany","DE",B.cC,"Same-sex marriage (Ehe f\xfcr alle) legal since October 1, 2017. Previously registered life partnerships (Lebenspartnerschaft) from 2001.",!0,"Apply at BAMF (Bundesamt f\xfcr Migration und Fl\xfcchtlinge). SOGI claims well-established. BAMF has SOGI-specialized decision-makers. Interview with trained officer. Appeal to Administrative Court (Verwaltungsgericht). Extensive case law.","Schwulenberatung Berlin, LesMigraS (Lesbenberatung Berlin), LSVD (Lesben- und Schwulenverband), Queer Refugees Deutschland.",!0,B.a2d,B.dA,"Very safe overall. Berlin is one of Europe's most LGBTQ+ friendly cities. Cologne, Hamburg, Munich also excellent. Christopher Street Day (CSD) celebrations nationwide. Some concerns about hate crimes rising in frequency though. Rural eastern Germany less accepting.",63,"Foreign same-sex marriages fully recognized. Family reunification for same-sex spouses. Residence permit for family reunion (Aufenthaltserlaubnis zum Familiennachzug). Registration at B\xfcrgeramt straightforward. Berlin, Cologne, Hamburg have largest LGBTQ+ immigrant communities.","Germany has the most extensive SOGI asylum infrastructure in the EU. Schwulenberatung Berlin operates dedicated shelter. BAMF SOGI competence centers in Nuremberg and branch offices. Queer Refugees Deutschland provides nationwide network. Major cities have specialized programs. Note: Dublin procedure may still apply.")
